==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|kaldr|lang=non}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈkʰaltʏr/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|altʏr|lang=is}}

===Adjective===
{{is-adj-01|köld|kalt|kaldari|kaldastur}}

# {{context|of a thing}} [[cold]]; having a [[low]] [[temperature]]
#: '''''Kalt''' járn.''
#:: '''Cold''' iron.
#: ''Mér er '''kalt''' á höndunum.''
#:: My hands are '''cold'''.
# {{context|of the weather}} [[cold]]; causing the [[air]] to be [[cold]]
# [[cold]]; [[unfriendly]], [[emotional]]ly distant or [[unfeeling]] 
#: '''''Köld''' augu.''
#:: '''Cold''' eyes.
#: '''''Kaldur''' svipur.''
#:: A '''cold''' look.
# [[cool]], [[calm]]

